<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:38Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>'From bad to catastrophic: Iran's justice system was already unfair for many decades'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6fb680832117ada2ecd2707ee74313a879c3cc0e01a7fe427e7257ecaa77dc2d</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T18:18:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/from-bad-to-catastrophic-iran-s-justice-system-was-already-unfair-for-many-decades--428389855ee7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/from-bad-to-catastrophic-iran-s-justice-system-was-already-unfair-for-many-decades" /><summary type="html">Amid war with the US and Israel, Iranian protesters continue to face death sentences following what Amnesty International describes as grossly unfair, torture-tainted trials. “The situation has changed from bad to catastrophic,” says Raha Bahreini, Iranian-Canadian human rights lawyer and Amnesty International's researcher on Iran. Bahreini discusses the aftermath of the January 2026 protests, the authorities' efforts to equate peaceful dissent with treason and espionage, and the extrajudicial killings of peaceful protesters. Amnesty International is calling for an international criminal justice mechanism, potentially a special tribunal. “There needs to be criminal accountability for these crimes against humanity.”</summary></entry><entry><title>With new law, Iraq sees rise in child marriage, custody battles</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25b9a28e8af4da5cdb50faf8066e23be99eb69a53a495c0c26e48126f4821ecc</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T14:48:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261127-with-new-law-iraq-sees-rise-in-child-marriage-custody-battles--d28ba6fc52bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261127-with-new-law-iraq-sees-rise-in-child-marriage-custody-battles" /><summary type="html">In January 2025, Iraq's parliament passed an amendment allowing families to place their household under religious law, governing all issues around marriage, divorce and inheritance. The new Ja'fari law, a Shiite law, came into force in October 2025. One year on, its consequences have been raising serious alarm, especially among women, who say they've seen a major rollback of their rights. FRANCE 24's Marie-Charlotte Roupie reports, with Josh Vardey.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's Eisenkot agrees to coalition deal with left-wing Democrats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3e1d09fdc1608acc7a02069f7623d1e17198747e63880d5d7a778bd387ff23b</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T06:46:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261127-israel-s-eisenkot-agrees-to-coalition-deal-with-left-wing-democrats--47f3c53a36e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261127-israel-s-eisenkot-agrees-to-coalition-deal-with-left-wing-democrats" /><summary type="html">Israel's former military chief Gadi Eisenkot on Thursday struck a coalition deal with Yair Golan's left-leaning Democrats, bringing the country's opposition closer to forming a government after no single bloc secured a majority in the October elections.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Hamas weighs response after Israel kills 10 people in Gaza</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1687cfab8ea0a8f415f683c8e590e122a116bd206facca75afc5444511a636b1</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T20:35:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/hamas-weighs-response-after-israel-kills-10-people-in-gaza--deb166341a81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/hamas-weighs-response-after-israel-kills-10-people-in-gaza" /><summary type="html">Five Israeli strikes and a shooting overnight and on Thursday killed 10 Palestinians across Gaza, according to officials at Shifa and Al-Aqsa Martyrs hospitals, where the casualties were taken. A strike on a residential apartment in Deir Al-Balah in central Gaza killed a man and his wife, the officials said. FRANCE 24's Jennie Shin speaks with journalist Ahmed Dremly, who was in Gaza until six months ago and has extensively covered the humanitarian crisis there.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel threatens to displace one million Palestinians in Gaza unless Hamas disarms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc645ec055475916135f29bf14260950032c2e4dd4a0d068ee5a873605d6e864</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T12:28:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261126-israel-threatens-to-displace-one-million-palestinians-in-gaza-unless-hamas-disarms--138d136f4246.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261126-israel-threatens-to-displace-one-million-palestinians-in-gaza-unless-hamas-disarms" /><summary type="html">Israel's defence minister on Thursday threatened to forcibly displace one million Palestinians in Gaza if Hamas does not move to voluntarily surrender its weapons, as previously promised.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iraqi court sentences 8 French nationals to life in prison for IS group membership</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbc8b9139d8451de935e8db9047cc877f84f996b6336a82f93348fe107690f93</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T06:28:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261126-iraqi-court-to-sentence-20-french-nationals-for-is-group-membership--de12edcfa160.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261126-iraqi-court-to-sentence-20-french-nationals-for-is-group-membership" /><summary type="html">An Iraqi court sentenced eight French nationals to life in prison and two others to 15 years on Thursday for joining the Islamic State group, as Baghdad steps up prosecutions of thousands of alleged jihadists transferred from Syria.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli lawmakers advance October 7 inquiry opposed by Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbcb8dd034ddf3f4043d390ea79d602a9fe5345ebe61d56796c8b1b802d4eec0</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T22:26:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israeli-lawmakers-advance-october-7-inquiry-opposed-by-netanyahu--52e0580706e5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-lawmakers-advance-october-7-inquiry-opposed-by-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">Israel's new parliament on Wednesday took a first step to set up a state commission of inquiry into the security failures that led to Hamas's unprecedented October 7, 2023 attack, a move long opposed by caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. FRANCE 24's Selina Sykes reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>In boost for Netanyahu, judges question corruption trial charges</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e639b0743ded033c6549eae39ea611188266ed1e7996abd43ea22f3e06881fb</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T19:28:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/in-boost-for-netanyahu-judges-question-corruption-trial-charges--4b586e8b77b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/in-boost-for-netanyahu-judges-question-corruption-trial-charges" /><summary type="html">Judges in the long-running corruption trial of Israeli caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu handed his defence a major boost on Wednesday in recommending the prosecution drop one of the cases in which he is accused of bribery. The recommendations, which came as Israel's longest-serving prime minister fights for his political survival, were immediately cheered by Netanyahu's right-wing allies who demanded the trial be brought to an end. FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem.</summary></entry><entry><title>Libya’s Haftar visits old foe Turkey for first time in ‘new phase’ of ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23949150cfd629189f2f4308fa6d42eaf1d1a695faf7293f14a6e3d585dfada5</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T15:19:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261125-libya-s-haftar-visits-old-foe-turkey-in-a-first-hails-new-phase-of-ties--e507ca73b955.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261125-libya-s-haftar-visits-old-foe-turkey-in-a-first-hails-new-phase-of-ties" /><summary type="html">Eastern Libya military commander Khalifa Haftar met Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan in Ankara on Wednesday during his first official visit to Turkey, marking a major thaw in relations between the longtime rivals. The visit came days after Ukraine struck a Russian warship in Benghazi, a port city controlled by Haftar.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli MPs advance bill for inquiry into security failings that led to October 7 Hamas attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c7a1874c60afef2a169a3c9296406aa873f1d7c4513370f4249aca7a3e9b2f0a</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T12:55:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261125-israeli-mps-advance-bill-for-inquiry-into-security-failings-that-led-to-october-7-hamas-att--b3ed77516c61.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261125-israeli-mps-advance-bill-for-inquiry-into-security-failings-that-led-to-october-7-hamas-attack" /><summary type="html">Israeli MPs on Wednesday gave their initial approval for the creation of a commission to investigate the security failures that led to the October 7, 2023 attack by Hamas. Caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, who was in power when the attack happened, has repeatedly rejected calls to set up such a probe.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Amnesty calls for ICC genocide probe over Israel's impact on births in Gaza</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca96c68515107d93d1679fb2c2baa88a5e9863fe7297dbda2c5765ff2367092f</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T04:01:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261125-amnesty-calls-for-icc-genocide-probe-over-israel-s-impact-on-births-in-gaza--37c802b616c9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261125-amnesty-calls-for-icc-genocide-probe-over-israel-s-impact-on-births-in-gaza" /><summary type="html">Amnesty International on Wednesday urged the International Criminal Court to investigate whether Israeli officials committed genocide in Gaza, citing measures it says have prevented births and severely harmed women's reproductive health. The rights group said it had serious concerns that these effects were intentional, while acknowledging it could not reach a definitive conclusion.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen’s army says Houthi fighters closing in on government stronghold of Aden</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dbdd47dd1ab38fd983c8d99628f41baf39fb05d1be9174515b01f39e05a6f0f1</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T16:51:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261124-yemen-army-houthi-attack-aden--d01a60ff9e63.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261124-yemen-army-houthi-attack-aden" /><summary type="html">Yemen's military on Tuesday said that Houthi fighters were closing in on the internationally recognised government's stronghold of Aden from about 60km (40 miles) away and vowed to repel any assault. A military spokesman said defences were prepared following Houthi advances and government pullbacks near the Red Sea.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>'We are ready to facilitate removal of Netanyahu': Head of Israel's Arab-majority Joint List</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a68e1221100c3c1e306526c63001ee367b75bd7ce68df3b09ef9b5f48736e6d</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T16:29:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261124-we-are-ready-to-facilitate-the-removal-of-netanyahu-from-power-head-of-israel-s-joint-list--73f044b29b95.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261124-we-are-ready-to-facilitate-the-removal-of-netanyahu-from-power-head-of-israel-s-joint-list" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, the head of the Arab-majority Joint List said his political alliance is prepared to play a decisive role in bringing down Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's government following the recent election. "We are ready to facilitate the removal of Netanyahu" from power, Yousef Jabareen said, signalling a willingness to explore political alliances beyond traditional divisions in Israeli politics.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli strikes on Gaza kill senior Hamas security official and six other people, medics say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bad75f1bddb5c97d36afa0e4dc73b17caa76272c736a8c3cf330e129c97d91e8</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T13:07:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261124-israeli-strikes-on-gaza-kill-senior-hamas-security-official-and-six-other-people-medics-say--d1ad5b170216.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261124-israeli-strikes-on-gaza-kill-senior-hamas-security-official-and-six-other-people-medics-say" /><summary type="html">Israeli air strikes on the devastated Gaza Strip killed Brigadier General Naeem Abu Nahel, director-general of the Palestinian territory's Internal Security Service on Tuesday, the ministry said. Another six people, including two police officers and a 17-year-old teenager, were killed in Israeli strikes across the enclave.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel’s Eisenkot slams ‘Jewish terrorism’ after attacks by settlers in West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2795a65dea659ed4023b7f73a13938af46c9c03c99720b37e207d704417662b0</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T21:29:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261122-israel-s-eisenkot-slams-jewish-terrorism-after-attacks-by-settlers-in-west-bank--d48459cb60f3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261122-israel-s-eisenkot-slams-jewish-terrorism-after-attacks-by-settlers-in-west-bank" /><summary type="html">Israeli opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot on Sunday condemned arson attacks by settlers on Palestinian villages in the West Bank as “Jewish terrorism”. Israeli police said they opened an investigation into the attacks, which came nearly a month after an inconclusive election stripped incumbent Prime Minister ⁠Benjamin Netanyahu of his majority.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>West Bank attacks: Opposition leader Eisenkot decries "Jewish terrorism"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c652734e5e2f07faa248df90dc4c99f000bb464006f0335747f3cbbdeae48f1</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T16:25:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/west-bank-attacks-opposition-leader-eisenkot-decries-jewish-terrorism--0689dfc975ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/west-bank-attacks-opposition-leader-eisenkot-decries-jewish-terrorism" /><summary type="html">Israeli authorities have opened an investigation after Palestinian vehicles and properties were set on fire in three villages in the occupied West Bank. Israeli soldiers were deployed to the area following the attacks, which local residents said were carried out by Israeli settlers. Gadi Eisenkot, a rival of outgoing Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, condemned the acts on X, describing them as “Jewish terrorism”. Antonia Kerrigan reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel investigates West Bank fires</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23055aab245576e9b14285397bf2e1799a15660f887f912b59494bca1389cbaf</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T13:47:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-investigates-west-bank-fires--de82d2e7e2ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-investigates-west-bank-fires" /><summary type="html">Israeli authorities have opened an investigation after Palestinian vehicles and properties were vandalised and set on fire in four villages in the occupied West Bank, in attacks local activists say were carried out by Israeli settlers. Around eight vehicles were reportedly torched and racist slogans sprayed on walls, prompting Israeli soldiers and police to deploy to the area. The attacks come amid a surge in settler violence since the outbreak of the Gaza war in October 2023, with more than 1,100 Palestinians killed by Israeli soldiers or settlers in the West Bank since then, according to an AFP tally. They also follow recent sanctions announced by the UK and Australia against eight Israeli companies involved in settlement activity. France 24 correspondent Noga Tarnopolsky shares further details from Jerusalem.</summary></entry><entry><title>Bahrain accuses Iran of striking industrial site as tankers hit in Hormuz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7dc43d8a73d5155e613ebaedfad4a2be3c253693b04bb79486c04658fe4da7d0</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T03:24:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261122-bahrain-accuses-iran-of-striking-industrial-site-as-tankers-hit-in-hormuz--f69cfc8e9d39.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261122-bahrain-accuses-iran-of-striking-industrial-site-as-tankers-hit-in-hormuz" /><summary type="html">Bahrain accused Iran of striking a civilian industrial site on Saturday evening, as two tankers were hit in the Strait of Hormuz. Tehran reported shooting down a US drone amid stalled efforts to end the war.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Eisenkot invites Netanyahu’s party for ‘marathon’ Israeli coalition talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e01d88e25a9662ef6419b4f3d5dccc17959b2254bf4d823887e7016bf24a64f9</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T20:49:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261121-eisenkot-invites-netanyahu-s-party-for-marathon-israeli-coalition-talks--1d2a83245b41.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261121-eisenkot-invites-netanyahu-s-party-for-marathon-israeli-coalition-talks" /><summary type="html">Israeli opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot has invited caretaker prime minister Benjamin Netanyahu's right-wing Likud party for coalition talks, his centrist Yashar party said Saturday. The "marathon series of talks" starts Sunday, the party said, adding that the move reflected a commitment to form "the broadest possible government" after the October election failed to deliver an outright winner.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Endurance athlete swims in Hormuz Strait</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb0aa1b285cc9d6e176cef10edf25a5fa146d87fe65fe2caa413b5a9fe58ad2c</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T16:02:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/endurance-athlete-swims-in-hormuz-strait--ff0cda0625e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/endurance-athlete-swims-in-hormuz-strait" /><summary type="html">The Strait of Hormuz remains largely blocked, with Iran attacking vessels attempting to cross it. As concerns grow over the environmental impact of the war, with toxic chemicals spreading through the air and sea, one swimmer and ocean advocate has gone a step further than issuing warnings: he plunged into the polluted and dangerous waters of the strait, calling on all sides to end the conflict.</summary></entry><entry><title>Houthis launch strikes on Saudi Arabia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7bd323c6140f6e61dbc6b0af8013f8e718bbad579c33c6e3ffcaa88be5955c9f</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T09:49:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/houthis-launch-strikes-on-saudi-arabia--258e24a13d6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/houthis-launch-strikes-on-saudi-arabia" /><summary type="html">Iran-backed Houthi rebels in Yemen continue to exchange strikes with the Saudi-led coalition. The coalition said it intercepted and destroyed three ballistic missiles fired towards Riyadh early on Saturday. It marks the second Houthi attack on the Saudi capital in recent days, following Saudi-led strikes on Houthi targets in Yemen. Yuka Royer has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen's Houthis target Riyadh after Saudi coalition's 'special operation'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e2278557731a975492914d15a0be06ff8c368c17751f4b4690e7c8868761231</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T18:36:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261120-yemen-s-houthis-target-riyadh-after-saudi-coalition-s-special-operation--562101e4c5eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261120-yemen-s-houthis-target-riyadh-after-saudi-coalition-s-special-operation" /><summary type="html">Yemen's Houthi rebels launched strikes on Riyadh on Saturday after Saudi-led coalition air raids on Yemen, escalating a months-long surge in cross-border attacks.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iraqi security forces deploy in Hezbollah stronghold under compromise deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a296d356df5e83b4c802b4b915c4ca550133332a8d948d634305fa347e2167e</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T08:37:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261120-iraqi-security-forces-to-deploy-in-hezbollah-stronghold-under-compromise-deal--1654847de472.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261120-iraqi-security-forces-to-deploy-in-hezbollah-stronghold-under-compromise-deal" /><summary type="html">Iraqi security forces deployed ​in the Kataib Hezbollah stronghold of Jurf al-Sakhar, state media said on Friday, under a compromise deal brokered by Shi'ite politicians. Iraq's prime minister ordered a security intervention earlier this week after accusing the Iran-backed militia of smuggling state-owned oil worth ⁠hundreds of millions of dollars.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Skyscraper in Riyadh damaged as Saudi Arabia reports surge in new Houthi attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bace047e2e31ab21a7f083cdcfcd44c71d1e990afe9fa117365a73a49e8ba0b4</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T07:58:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261119-skyscraper-in-riyadh-damaged-as-saudi-arabia-reports-surge-in-new-houthi-attacks--e54170cb555f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261119-skyscraper-in-riyadh-damaged-as-saudi-arabia-reports-surge-in-new-houthi-attacks" /><summary type="html">A skyscraper in Saudi Arabia's capital Riyadh was damaged on Thursday after the Gulf country reported new attacks by Yemen's Houthis. Witnesses said the city's Public Investment Fund Tower, which showcases Saudi Arabia's economic ambitions, was "damaged across several floors, with windows blown out".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Gaza: Israel launched new offensive on Nuseirat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:74a7cb8d7d01258b56357012e355690c2f5255d0bfc0b4c1220586c3cafc468d</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T07:50:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/gaza-israel-launched-new-offensive-on-nuseirat--5e7b3fc17c6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/gaza-israel-launched-new-offensive-on-nuseirat" /><summary type="html">Israeli tanks have moved east of the Nuseirat refugee camp in central Gaza, with witnesses reporting heavy shelling, gunfire and airstrikes as the Israeli military says it has launched an operation in a Hamas-controlled area. Strikes killed at least three people on Wednesday, and displaced families are fleeing again, saying there is no real ceasefire. Israel and Hamas accuse each other of breaking the truce in force since October 2025, while Gadi Eisenkot tries to form a government after inconclusive elections.</summary></entry><entry><title>Middle East crisis poses 'largest threat' to energy security in history, warns IEA</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f37b134f6ed50aeb61c174f741f7359c158f2d49b1401b040772374aaed547b7</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T05:11:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261119-middle-east-crisis-energy-security-iea--bef2931d058a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261119-middle-east-crisis-energy-security-iea" /><summary type="html">The International Energy Agency said on Thursday that the Middle East crisis triggered by US and Israeli strikes on Iran in February posed the “largest threat” to energy security in history. It warned that consumers were bearing more of the costs as Iran’s blockade of the Strait of Hormuz disrupted oil shipments.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli army launches ground operation in Hamas-controlled area of Gaza</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e72aefc9b5ae04acb72f3f4dabcf0c623b6623d5ff1c32953cb36892e12c016f</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T19:55:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israeli-army-launches-ground-operation-in-hamas-controlled-area-of-gaza--842ad9ad2dc7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-army-launches-ground-operation-in-hamas-controlled-area-of-gaza" /><summary type="html">The Israeli military said it had launched an operation on Wednesday in a Hamas-controlled area of central Gaza, where an AFP journalist saw Israeli tanks position themselves east of the Nuseirat refugee camp. The rare ground operation comes after inconclusive Israeli elections, with the opposition's Gadi Eisenkot trying to form a government without caretaker prime minister Benjamin Netanyahu, who has built his brand on saying he will ensure Israel's security. FRANCE 24's Daniel Whittington reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Writer Etgar Keret: 'The Israel my parents dreamed of' is still possible, but not under Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e92beeb93ce25375ea819e2f8a631cad86456f8cbe641a9bf12b66fc0809d54</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T19:45:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261118-netanyahu-s-only-2-tickets-are-racism-or-starting-a-war-he-stopped-acting-as-a-democratic-p--f0085602677a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261118-netanyahu-s-only-2-tickets-are-racism-or-starting-a-war-he-stopped-acting-as-a-democratic-player" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Israeli writer and filmmaker Etgar Keret, author of "The Seven Good Years". Keret argues that Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu is seeking to remain in power, at any cost, including delegitimising Arab parties and prolonging conflict. "For him, it could be a never-ending war as long as he's in power. He has no incentive to stop it," our guest warns.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Gazans flee shelters as Israeli army launches ground operation beyond Yellow Line</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e18dc44f5f1f086cfca3efe062761e4085e000c66a904539faae48649c42acf1</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T16:03:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-gazans-flee-shelters-as-israeli-army-launches-ground-operation-beyond-yellow-line--9caf8473edb4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-gazans-flee-shelters-as-israeli-army-launches-ground-operation-beyond-yellow-line" /><summary type="html">Palestinians fled their tents and shelters in central Gaza on Wednesday after Israel launched a rare ground operation in an area it withdrew ​from under a ‌2025 ceasefire. The Israeli army said it crossed the Yellow Line separating Israeli and Hamas-controlled areas "to remove a threat posed to IDF troops operating in the Gaza Strip".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Why the Houthis may besiege Aden rather than storm it</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6dcf1cd78408be115fe9eadedd427c7f9ba6a14f48b3a50b909137874c589c19</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:55:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-yemen-why-the-houthis-may-besiege-aden-rather-than-storm-it--cc45be20d135.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-yemen-why-the-houthis-may-besiege-aden-rather-than-storm-it" /><summary type="html">Bolstered by their recent military successes, Houthi rebels this week advanced close to the southern port city of Aden, the interim capital of the internationally recognised Yemeni government. Amid territorial ambitions, regional rivalries, and divisions within government forces, the potential fall of this stronghold could permanently alter the balance of power in the country.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry></feed>
